- Topical antibiotic ointment (A) is not indicated for a Stage I pressure ulcer, as it is not infected yet.
- Radiation therapy (B), antifungal treatment (C), broad-spectrum antibiotics (D), corticosteroid cream (E), surgical debridement (G), cryotherapy (I), and whirlpool therapy (J) are not appropriate for a Stage I pressure ulcer.

The answer is **(H)**.
